From 1f56efe1e4a1af461693a13ef052c3179e75c07b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Karl Mehltretter <kmehltretter@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 03:48:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] KVM: arm64: Reject empty SMCCC filter ranges

The SMCCC filter UAPI defines ranges as [base, base + nr_functions).
An existing selftest expects a zero function count to fail with
-EINVAL.

The wrap check catches a zero count for every nonzero base, but base
zero underflows the inclusive end to U32_MAX without satisfying
end < start. KVM then attempts to insert the accidental full-ID range,
which collides with the reserved architecture ranges, so the ioctl fails
with -EEXIST instead of -EINVAL.

Reject a zero function count explicitly.

Verified with a small userspace reproducer on an arm64 KVM host using VHE
under QEMU TCG: EEXIST before this change, EINVAL afterward.

Fixes: 821d935c87bc ("KVM: arm64: Introduce support for userspace SMCCC filtering")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Karl Mehltretter <kmehltretter@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/kvm/hypercalls.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kvm/hypercalls.c b/arch/arm64/kvm/hypercalls.c
index b11b8821c9fbc..dfa25bb6f25d4 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kvm/hypercalls.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kvm/hypercalls.c
@@ -185,7 +185,8 @@ static int kvm_smccc_set_filter(struct kvm *kvm, struct kvm_smccc_filter __user
 	start = filter.base;
 	end = start + filter.nr_functions - 1;
 
-	if (end < start || filter.action >= NR_SMCCC_FILTER_ACTIONS)
+	if (!filter.nr_functions || end < start ||
+	    filter.action >= NR_SMCCC_FILTER_ACTIONS)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	mutex_lock(&kvm->arch.config_lock);

